# Normalise line endings, and check every text file out as LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git's core.autocrlf (on by default on Windows) rewrites text
# files to CRLF at checkout. The blobs stay LF, so nothing looks wrong in a
# diff, but the bytes on disk differ from the bytes CI sees. A test that
# asserts on file content then fails only on Windows, only in a fresh clone.
# That is exactly what happened: body.startsWith('---\n') in test/ai.test.ts
# is false once the checkout produced ---\r\n.
#
# The templates are the other reason. psk new copies them verbatim into a
# user's project, so their line endings should not depend on the platform
# the package was built on.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
